{"skill":{"slug":"graphic-design","displayName":"Graphic Design"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770760812056,"changelog":"Initial release","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6669,"sha256":"20d17669d814027529c9011eb0431f5439be8f6f13a03ed283e992640ec0885a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1976,"sha256":"5dfa02b417fb360974e59055de9a1ca7fa81cabbc935462525851220cfc15195","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":false,"checkedAt":1789059514971,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"1dc6e5cddde42724af4d8358ea2ce90f20b97f59cc77ff5dbb4dff1ba86fe23b","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/1dc6e5cddde42724af4d8358ea2ce90f20b97f59cc77ff5dbb4dff1ba86fe23b","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: graphic-design\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe OpenClaw skill bundle contains only a metadata file and a markdown file (`SKILL.md`). The `SKILL.md` file provides detailed instructions for an AI agent on how to act as a graphic design assistant, covering various aspects from basic principles to professional production and theory. There are no executable scripts, shell commands, network calls, file system operations, or any instructions that suggest data exfiltration, persistence, or other malicious activities. The content is entirely focused on providing design guidance and lacks any prompt injection attempts designed to subvert the agent for harmful purposes.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162978421},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":7,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1789059514971},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a plain graphic-design guidance skill with no executable code, privileged access, persistence, or hidden behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill does not request local file access, credentials, network calls, command execution, or broad environment authority; references to Canva and Coolors are ordinary user-facing design tool suggestions.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The package contains a single non-executable Markdown skill file plus simple metadata; no install scripts, dependencies, hooks, or remote payloads were present.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Directive wording such as enforce, flag, demand, and provide is scoped to design coaching and production review, not system control, user impersonation, destructive actions, or bypassing safeguards.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No persistence, privilege escalation, memory writing, background agents, scheduled tasks, or tool modification behavior appears in the artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact's stated purpose is graphic design support, and its instructions stay within advice, critique, specifications, accessibility, print production, and workflow guidance.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"This skill is appropriate for general design guidance. Users should treat tool and template recommendations as suggestions and verify professional production requirements such as print bleeds, CMYK, and accessibility contrast for their specific project.","findings":"[EA2] expected: The flagged phrase relates to giving common design size specifications without first asking follow-up questions. That is purpose-aligned design advice, not autonomous high-impact action or unsafe execution.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789059514971}}}}}